Third-party notices
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section reproduces the notices that the licences of third-party code
or data copied into this repository require. Each entry names the component,
its source and commit as recorded in PROVENANCE.md, its copyright line and its
licence. A component under Apache-2.0 also brings the contents of its own
NOTICE file.

None yet. No third-party code or data that needs a notice has been copied
into this repository.

Code copied from inflect-compliance is not third-party code: it is BUSL-1.1
from the same Licensor, Inflect Ltd. (ADR 0001, decision D1), and
PROVENANCE.md records each copied file. Third-party material inside that code
brings its notice here in the same change that copies it. Two are planned:

- Dub (github.com/dubinc/dub), "Copyright (c) 2024-present Dub Technologies,
  Inc.", licensed AGPL-3.0 outside Dub's (ee) folders; and the Nucleo icon
  notice ("Copyright © Nucleo"; redistribution of the icons is prohibited;
  they are restricted for use only within the product they are bundled with;
  nucleoapp.com/license). Both are added with packages/ui in sub-phase 1.2,
  per ADR 0001 decision D4. Neither is in the repository today.
- pipelock (Apache-2.0), added with a port of the AI guard (sub-phase 6.1).

npm dependencies are not copied into the repository. Each package carries its
own licence and notice files under node_modules, and scripts/licence-gate.mjs
checks the production dependency tree against the licence allowlist on every
pull request. The container image built in sub-phase 1.8 carries the LGPL
notice for the libvips binaries that sharp loads, and this file gains an entry
for them in the same change (ADR 0007, decision E1a).
